<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak '96 tourist revenues rise to $672.8 mln.</title>
<headline>Slovak '96 tourist revenues rise to $672.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Revenues from tourists coming into Slovakia rose to $672.8 million in 1996, from $629.0 million for the previous year, the Economics Ministry said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that 33.1 million foreigners visited Slovakia last year, a 21.2 percent increase, year-on-year.</p>
<p>It added that 22.9 million Slovaks travelled abroad in 1996, a 27.2 percent rise year-on-year, spending some $482.8 million.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
